{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And the serpent was cunning.</b> One must say that by happenstance previously it had eaten from the tree of knowledge, since the warning was only to the human." "<b>And he said to the woman.</b> The Holy One, blessed be He, opened the mouth of the serpent just as He opened the mouth of Balaam's donkey." "<b>Even though Elohim said</b> etc. Even if HaShem, blessed be He, stated His commandment — you shall not eat of any tree in the garden — in wonderment, according to reason she too knew the command, as it is written <b>even though Elohim said, you shall not eat</b> etc."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:02:35.783330169Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}